        "evidence": "Reads aloud cleanly.",
        "notes": "VERIFIED, all correct. The two composition identities check symbolically: 1/(1 - 1/(1-z)) = (1-z)/(-z) = 1 - 1/z, and 1 - (1-z) = z, so z -> 1/(1-z) does cycle the three edge parameters as claimed. The volume claim follows since vol = Lambda(theta_1) + Lambda(theta_2) + Lambda(theta_3) is cycle-symmetric -- and note the block uses Lambda correctly here (the Lobachevsky form of the ideal-tetrahedron volume), so this is not an instance of the Lambda-vs-Cl_2 guard. The 5_2 consequence also checks: D is invariant on the cyclic orbit {z, 1/(1-z), 1-1/z}, so shapes (y_1, 1/(1-y_1), y_1) sum to 3 D(y_1). The law of sines |z| = sin(theta_2)/sin(theta_3) is the standard relation. Minor notation nit: the modulus is written with a double bar, ||z||, where |z| is meant."
      }
